<title>GERMANY: Lafontaine says EMU stability pact not needed.</title>
<headline>Lafontaine says EMU stability pact not needed.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oskar Lafontaine, leader of Germany's opposition Social Democrats (SPD), said on Monday the stability pact for European monetary union (EMU) was not needed because inflation was low.</p>
<p>Lafontaine also said he opposed taking too narrow an interpretation of the Maastricht criteria for EMU participation, adding that the three percent limit of debt to economic output was not written in the treaty.</p>
</text>
